  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Phase 4 — task UI (AC 18-26)
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI1 The task-ui classifies every unit only from the status tags
    Given a status with waiting, active, trusted, dead, blocked and cancelled tasks
    When the Board and the counts read it
    Then waiting tasks are in WAITING, active tasks in the column of their phase, stopped tasks in STOPPED and the other ended tasks in TRUSTED
    And STOPPED groups dead tasks, then blocked tasks, then the rest
    And the counts, the focus and the next running task come from the tags
    And the task-ui keeps no list of active or ended state names

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI2 The task-ui view state is one machine
    Given the task-ui plugin started for a session
    When the user switches design, selects a task, expands, watches and presses the stop key once
    Then the design, the selection, the expansion, the watch target and the stop-key arming are states and context of one view machine
    And the stop key disarms 5 seconds after it was armed
    And the status, session list, activity lines and proof-log tail are read by delayed transitions every 1 s, 2 s, 1.5 s and 500 ms
    And a status text that does not parse keeps the last good status

  @phase4 @permissions @ops
  Scenario: UI3 Liveness comes from the status tags and the heartbeat
    Given a status file
    When the run lacks the ended tag and its heartbeat is at most 15 seconds old
    Then the view is live, and Tab, esc twice and the watch keys act on the run when the session owns its harness sessions
    And an older or absent heartbeat makes the view still, an ended run makes it ended, and no file makes it absent
    And the run keys leave a run alone when the view is not live or the session does not own it

  @phase4 @core @edge @ASSUMPTION:A2.a
  Scenario: UI4 The Gantt draws each lane from the task's spans
    Given a status whose tasks carry spans
    When the Gantt renders
    Then each cell shows the span that holds its middle time, and the cells before the first span are blank
    And an open span runs to now while live and to the heartbeat while still
    And a final state with no length takes one cell, and a blocked task shows one warning cell

  @phase4 @core @edge
  Scenario: UI5 An outside wait and an external wait read differently
    Given a waiting task whose waitingOn holds the untrusted outside id T9 and the external id T1.1
    When the Board card, the Peek and the collapsed views render
    Then the outside wait reads "waiting on T9 (outside) — run /task trust T9" on every design, and the shortcut bar has an outside-wait part
    And the external wait reads "waiting on T1.1 (not in this run)" with no trust command

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI6 The run header shows the spec title
    Given the release-notes spec, whose title is "Release notes from conventional commits"
    When /task starts a whole-spec run and a subtree run
    Then the first message reads "Implementing spec" and the title, from structured header metadata
    And the transcript draws "Implementing spec" muted and the title bold, from that metadata
    And a subtree run reads "Implementing" with the task id and title, then "from spec" and the spec title
    And an empty title falls back to the spec id, and the status run carries the title and, for a subtree run, the task
    And a subtree run that leaves scenarios out adds the muted line "Left out: <ids> — they need tasks outside this run."
    And an older header in the scrollback keeps its own title when a later run starts

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI7 A closing summary appears in the transcript when the run ends
    Given a run that ends with a dead task, a blocked task, a rejected scenario and a parked scenario
    When the run machine reaches a final state
    Then the root session gets one assistant-role markdown message with no model call
    And it holds the outcome line, the counts line with the duration, tokens and cost, the stopped tasks with their reasons, the scenarios that did not pass with their reasons, the scenarios not run, and a table of every task's duration
    And it holds the run-warning line when the spec stopped validating during the run

  @phase4 @core @edge
  Scenario: UI8 The summary is written even when a turn is in flight or the run was cancelled
    Given a root session with a turn in flight
    When the run ends, or the user aborts the root session, or the run is cancelled
    Then the summary waits for the turn and is then written once
    And a later user prompt in the root session still runs a model turn

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI9 Failure reasons appear in every expanded view and in the Peek heading
    Given a status with a budget-exhausted task, a failed task and a blocked task
    When each of the seven designs is expanded
    Then the shared region lists each stopped task with its reason or upstream cause
    And the Peek BUILDER heading shows the selected task's reason in full, wrapped
    And the collapsed views keep only the glyph

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI10 Every expanded view lists the run's scenarios
    Given the release-notes status with thirteen scenarios, titles, one rejected scenario and one parked scenario
    When each of the seven designs is expanded at 120 by 40 cells
    Then the shared region lists S1 to S13 with glyph, id, state label and title
    And the rejected scenario shows its reason under its entry
    And after the run ends the parked scenario reads "not run"

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI11 Each task shows its duration where the UX document places it
    Given a status with a running task, an ended task and a task that never started
    When the designs render while the run is live
    Then the running task's duration counts from its start, the ended task's is fixed, and the unstarted task's is blank
    And durations appear in the Gantt right column, the Matrix time column, the Board card, the HUD selected-task line and the Peek heading
    And a duration reads "45s", "3m 12s" or "1h 4m"

  @phase4 @edge @ASSUMPTION:A2.a
  Scenario: UI12 A run that stands still freezes its durations and its diamond (default 6, pending ruling)
    Given a status whose heartbeat is older than 15 seconds and whose run has not ended
    When the task-ui renders
    Then a running task's duration stops at the heartbeat time
    And the diamond is a static ◆

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI13 The shortcut bar no longer shows the task-design switch hint
    Given a live run in any design
    When the shortcut bar renders
    Then it shows no "/task-design switch" part
    And /task-design still switches designs from the command list

  @phase4 @core @accessibility
  Scenario: UI14 The In the Flow diamond grows and melts while the run is live
    Given a live run
    When any In the Flow mark renders
    Then its diamond plays the frames · ⬩ ⬪ ⬥ ◆ ⬥ ⬪ ⬩ at about 120 ms each through the spinner element
    And it is a static ◆ when the run has ended or animations are off
    And the Peek border title and the toast title stay static
    And the diamond is not bold in either form

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI15 The run's tokens and cost are shown for a /task root session
    Given a /task root session whose child harness sessions spent tokens
    When the prompt footer, the sidebar and the task-ui render
    Then each shows the summed tokens and cost of the child sessions, live
    And nothing shows before any harness session reports tokens, and other sessions are unchanged
    And a free model that spent tokens shows "$0.00", and a narrow footer drops the root's own figure, then the word tokens
    And the closing summary repeats the run total

  @phase4 @ops
  Scenario: UI16 A run warning shows in the task-ui and goes when the spec validates again
    Given a status with a run warning of two failures
    When the task-ui renders
    Then every run-state surface shows "! spec no longer validates · 2 failures"
    And the shared region lists each failure line
    And a warning toast appears once, and the warning goes from every surface when the status loses it

  @phase4 @negative
  Scenario: UI17 A refused run shows every reason in the task-ui
    Given a refused status with three failure lines
    When the Ledger and a full-screen design render
    Then the Ledger shows "run: refused" and every failure line
    And the full-screen body reads "No work started: the spec was refused." with every failure line

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI18 A blocked unit has its own glyph and tone
    Given a status with a blocked task and a blocked scenario
    When the designs render
    Then the blocked units show ⊖ in the warning tone
    And the Matrix legend lists "⊖ blocked"
    And a Ticker toast for a task that turns blocked shows its reason

  @phase4 @ops
  Scenario: UI19 The not-run line of a done run is muted and raises no notification
    Given a done status whose reason is "not run: S13 waits on T8"
    When the Ledger, the full-screen header and the Ticker render
    Then the run reason line uses the muted tone, and the Ticker raises no notification for it
    And a run with the stopped tag shows its reason line in the error tone

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI20 The summary outcome line follows the outcome rules (owner ruling 1)
    Given final statuses for a cancel, a dead task, a rejected scenario with every task trusted, a done run with one parked scenario, and a subtree run
    When each summary is built
    Then the outcome lines read "— cancelled: <first reason line>", "— budget exhausted", "— failed: acceptance not proved" and "— done · 1 scenario not run"
    And the subtree summary starts with the task id and title, then "from spec" and the spec title
    And a spec that stopped validating and then validated again still gives the run-warning line

  @phase4 @core
  Scenario: UI21 The stopped count, the idle watch band, the did-not-start Peek and the empty scenario list read as set
    Given a status with 2 stopped tasks, a run waiting only on T9, a cancelled task with no start time, and no scenarios
    When the designs, the watch band and the Peek render
    Then each trusted count ends with "· 2 stopped" in the error tone, and shows nothing at 0
    And the watch band reads "Nothing is running. The run is waiting on T9 (outside) — run /task trust T9."
    And the Peek reads "no builder session: the task did not start"
    And the SCENARIOS heading reads "SCENARIOS none in this run"

  @phase4 @accessibility
  Scenario: UI22 Every entry of the shared region stays reachable
    Given a full-screen design at 120 by 24 cells with 13 scenarios and 5 stopped tasks
    When the user presses pagedown and clicks a STOPPED line
    Then the region keeps at least 8 rows, the Peek activity lines shrink first, and every entry is reachable by scroll
    And the click selects the first task of the line
    And under 149 cells the Board's right pane sits below the board

  @phase4 @negative
  Scenario: UI23 A summary that cannot be written does not hold the run open
    Given a run whose root session was deleted before the run ends
    When the run machine reaches a final state
    Then the failed say is logged
    And the run supervisor reaches closed, the job ends and the directory lease is released
    And the next /task in the directory is not busy
